  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14199831/assets/8fca4f1d297c465ecf9da9bef652f1602edb6e6cd8887f6b3b8a83441a40871b.png)\n\nThe two quadrilaterals shown above are similar. What is the correct similarity statement?",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's find the measures of unknown angles. Since the sum of the measures of internal angles of a quadrilateral is ${360}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠R+m∠T+m∠U+m∠V & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠R+{130}^{∘}+{50}^{∘}+{110}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠R+{290}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠R & ={70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠O+m∠N+m∠Q+m∠P & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {70}^{∘}+{130}^{∘}+m∠Q+{110}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠Q+{310}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠Q & ={50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the quadrilaterals are similar, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠R≅∠O,\\,∠T≅∠N,\\,∠U≅∠Q,\\,∠V≅∠P.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that \n\n- $R$ corresponds to $O,$\n\n- $T$ corresponds to $N,$\n\n- $U$ corresponds to $Q,$\n\n- $V$ corresponds to $P.$\n\nTherefore, $RTUV∼ONQP.$",
